## Build and run the image

cd project
docker build -t my-website .
docker run -d -p 8080:80 --name my-site-name imagename:tag

## Bind a data saveing place

Use $(pwd) for the current directory
**docker run -v "$(pwd)/data":/app/data myimage\*\*

Long syntax (--mount): more explicit, recommended
**docker run --mount type=bind,source=/home/user/data,target=/app/data myimage**

## Docker Compose:

services:
app: # service name (your choice)
image: nginx:latest # image to use
container_name: myapp # optional fixed name
ports: - "8080:80" # host:container
environment: - TZ=Europe/Zurich
volumes: - ./data:/usr/share/nginx/html # bind mount: host folder : container path
restart: unless-stopped

## Commands to run

docker compose up -d # start in the background
docker compose ps # see running containers
docker compose logs -f # follow logs
docker compose down # stop and remove the containers
